---
date added: 2026-10-30
title: Bacon, Egg & Cheese Quiche
author: King Arthur Baking
source: https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/bacon-egg-cheese-quiche-recipe
tags: quiche, eggs, breakfast, brunch, make-ahead, pie crust
servings: 10
time required: 1 hour 25 minutes
notes: Crust is King Arthur's Classic Single Pie Crust (https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/classic-single-pie-crust-recipe). To use leftover cubed ham, swap about 2 cups of ham for the bacon — it's already cooked, so skip the bacon-frying step. Don't overfill the crust; bake any extra filling in a custard cup.
---

== Crust ==

In a medium #bowl{}, whisk together the @all-purpose flour{180%g}(or 170g pastry flour blend) and @table salt{1/2%teaspoon}.

Add the @vegetable shortening{46%g}, working it in until the mixture is evenly crumbly.

Add the @unsalted butter{71%g}(cold) to the flour mixture, and work it in roughly with your fingers, a #pastry cutter{}, or a mixer. Don't be too thorough; the mixture should be very uneven, with big chunks of butter in among the smaller ones.

Add 28g of @ice water{43-71%g}, and toss to combine.

Toss with enough additional water to make a chunky mixture. It should barely hold together when you squeeze a handful, though the remainder may look quite dry.

Shape the dough into a disk about 1" thick, and refrigerate it for ~{30%minutes} or longer; this resting period allows the flour to absorb the water, making the dough easier to roll out. If you decide to let the dough chill longer than 30 minutes allow it rest at room temperature for 10 to 15 minutes before rolling, to allow the butter to soften up a bit.

When you're "ready to roll," remove the dough from the fridge. Roll the dough to the size needed (about 12" for a 9" pie). Place it in a #9" pie pan{}, and refrigerate it while you prepare your filling.

== Quiche ==

Preheat the oven to 375°F.

For the crust: Roll the prepared pie dough into a 12" circle (to fit a 9" pie pan). Prick it all over with a fork. Bake the crust for ~{10%minutes}, then remove it from the oven and set it aside to cool.

To make the filling: Cook the @bacon{340%g} in a #frying pan{} until crisp. Let it cool on a paper towel-lined plate. Once cool, roughly chop it up.

Dice the @yellow onion{340%g}(1 large, peeled) into medium-sized pieces (about 1/2"). Melt the @butter{28%g} in a #saucepan{} over medium heat and add the onion. Season to taste with @salt{} and @pepper{}. Cook until the onion has softened and is just starting to brown. Remove it from the heat and set it aside.

In a large bowl, whisk together the @heavy cream{170%g}, @milk{57%g}, and @large eggs{6}. Add the bacon, onions, @Cabot Alpine Cheddar{170%g}(grated), @table salt{1/4%teaspoon}, and @ground black pepper{1/4%teaspoon}. Pour the mixture into the pie crust. Don't overfill! If you find you have too much filling, just leave a little out, baking it alongside the pie in a custard cup, if desired.

Bake the quiche for about ~{40%minutes}. The edges should be golden brown and the center should feel just set.

Remove the quiche from the oven and let it cool on a rack. Serve warm, or at room temperature. Refrigerate any leftovers.
